# Server / API

## Architecture

**Next.js only** — no separate Express app. Auth, portfolio CRUD, and public data live in:

- Route Handlers under `src/app/api/`
- and/or Server Actions

## Today

Clerk owns authentication (email/password + Google). Local Mongo `User` syncs by `clerkId`. Set `MONGODB_URI` + Clerk keys.

## Stack

Next.js Route Handlers + Mongoose + MongoDB Atlas · Clerk sessions · Upstash rate limits (optional)

## Collections

**users:** clerkId (unique), email (unique), isEmailVerified, deletedAt, timestamps  

**portfolios:** userId (unique), title, slug (unique), status `draft|published`, paletteId, optional customPalette (5 hex tokens), embedded `sections[]` (`id`, `type`, `order`, `visible`, `variant` 1–6, `data`), publishedAt, timestamps

Section types: Header, Hero, About, Skills, Projects, CTA, Experience, Education, Contact, Footer (at most one each). Clamp `variant` to 1 for non-variant types.

## Endpoints

- Auth: `GET /api/auth/me`, `DELETE /api/auth/account` (soft-delete + Clerk ban); sign-in/up via Clerk UI
- Portfolio: get/create (409 if exists), patch, delete, slug availability/change, publish/unpublish
- Public: published portfolio by slug (for `/{slug}` SSR)

## Rules

- Validate inputs (Zod)
- Rate-limit slug checks
- Soft-deleted users cannot authenticate; free their slug on account delete
- One portfolio per user enforced at DB unique index + application layer
- Do not reintroduce a separate `api/` Express package
